1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,410
Two Edmonton neighbours share a wall, and their mortgages renew the same month.

2
00:00:04,450 --> 00:00:07,900
But in five years, one of them pays thousands more in interest.

3
00:00:07,950 --> 00:00:12,210
The left side waits for the bank's letter, which can come just 21 days out.

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,590
So they sign off on the first offer.

5
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:17,360
The right side starts four months early.

6
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:20,060
Renewing in March? Day 120 is about now.

7
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:23,010
They get other lenders to hold a rate, then compare.

8
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,060
Say the first offer is half a point higher.

9
00:00:26,100 --> 00:00:28,310
That's about $80 a month.

10
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:30,510
Over five years? What's your guess?

11
00:00:32,250 --> 00:00:35,070
About $7,000 more in interest.

12
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:38,600
Keith Crosland and Dustin Moss spent years inside big banks.

13
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:41,350
They treat the first offer as a starting point.

14
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,050
Send this to the neighbour renewing next.
